{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Ask your father</b> — a hint to those who understand, and likewise <b>your elders</b>. The reason is as it says (Deuteronomy 4:19), \"whom YHWH your Elohim has allotted,\" and so forth, for every portion below has a corresponding portion above, and the reason for <b>the number of the children of Israel</b> is that the form of Jacob is engraved upon the throne of glory, and this is a great secret. And the proof is <b>for the portion of YHWH is His people</b>, and this is a great distinction that He did not do so for any other nation. Therefore it says, <b>Is it to YHWH that you repay this, O foolish and unwise people</b>, who fell from his distinction in his folly. And this is the meaning of <b>your father acquired you</b>, for he acquired him for His glory and taught him, as he will explain in the matter of a father with a son — the language of R. Abraham ibn Ezra (on Deuteronomy 32:6). And the words of a wise man are gracious. If so, the interpretation of <b>Remember the days of eternity</b> is that they should set their heart to remember the six days of Genesis, the goodness He did for them at the time of formation, as it says, <b>When the Most High gave the nations their inheritance</b>, and so forth. <b>Understand the years of generation after generation</b> — that they should understand and know what was done for them throughout the generations from the time the Shekhinah dwelt among them, as he will recount: <b>He found him in a desert land</b>, and so forth. And Rashi wrote (on Deuteronomy 32:10), <b>He found him in a desert land</b> — He found them faithful to Him in the desert land, for they accepted upon themselves His Torah and His sovereignty and His yoke, which Ishmael and Esau did not do. <b>In the howling waste of a wilderness</b> — a land of drought and desolation, a place of the howling of jackals and ostriches; even there they pursued faith, and did not say to Moses, \"How shall we go out into the wilderness?\" But this is not the reason of the passage, for Scripture rebukes Israel, and recalls the kindnesses that HaShem did with them while they repaid Him with evil for good:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "In the phrase 'as he will explain in the matter of a father with a son,' Ramban refers to Ibn Ezra's interpretation of יכרנו in verse 6 as קנה in the sense of a parent raising a child; the pronoun 'he' refers to Ibn Ezra."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:58:10.446400409Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}